efusal comes from the kernel rests on the marker alone, which no path was found for the confined\n+      code to learn.\n+    what_expected: >\n+      Only a line the kernel publishes is read: a message logged by a confined process, whatever its name and whatever\n+      it carries, never reaches the reading, marker or not.\n+    steps_to_reproduce:\n+      - \"Build an executable named `Sandbox` that logs `Sandbox: node(1) deny(1) file-write-create /forged/path\\\\n<marker>` through os_log, and run it under `sandbox-exec` with a profile of 495.\"\n+      - \"Read `log show --style ndjson --predicate 'sender == \\\"Sandbox\\\"'`: the forged line is there with `processID` the probe's pid and `senderImagePath` the probe's path; the kernel's own refusals carry `processID` 0, `processImagePath` `/kernel` and `senderImagePath` `/System/Library/Extensions/Sandbox.kext/Contents/MacOS/Sandbox`.\"\n+      - \"Remove `sender == \\\"Sandbox\\\" AND` from the predicate: `test/v1-adapters/seatbelt-refused-writes.test.ts` stays green.\"\n+    root_cause: >\n+      The predicate names the sender by its image name rather than by what only the kernel has (`processID == 0`, or the\n+      kext's `senderImagePath`), and no test sends a line from another image. Introduced by the branch e40s03.\n+    evidence: >\n+      Probed during the review of the branch e40s03 by a reviewer: the forged line reached a `log stream` under the\n+      predicate 495 uses, `senderImagePath=/private/tmp/…/Sandbox`. Read again on 2026-10-12 with `log show`: the forged\n+      line carries `processID` 78795 and `/private/tmp/a1probe/Sandbox`, a kernel refusal `processID` 0 and `/kernel`.\n+      No forged line was carried into an evidence end to end, the marker not being found from inside the confinement\n+      (`ps` refused, `log` refuses to run confined).\n+    risk_level: medium\n+    follow_ups: >\n+      Add `processID == 0` (or `senderImagePath` of the kext) to the predicate, and hold it with a test 